          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A premonoidal category is a generalisation of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Power"} John Power
            and his collaborators to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/denotational+semantics"} denotational semantics
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+science"} computer science
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strong monad
            provides a model of
            %span.newWikiWord
              call-by-value
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/call-by-value"} ?
            programming languages. In general, if the original category is monoidal, the Kleisli category will only be premonoidal.
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifunctor"} bifunctor
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C,D,E
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \times D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y,Z
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            in each variable yet not
            %span.newWikiWord
              jointly continuous
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/jointly+continuous+function"} ?
            (continuous from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+product"} Tychonoff product
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \times Z
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with a bifunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \times C \to C
            (equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            such as the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \times C \to C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            as shown, but one which need only be functorial in each variable separately.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong binoidal category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with
          %ul
            %li
              for each pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes y
            %li
              for each object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \rtimes -
              whose action on objects sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes y
            %li
              for each object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⋉
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \ltimes x
              whose action on objects sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \otimes x
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon x \to y
            in a binoidal category is
            %strong central
            if, for every morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'\colon x' \to y'
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ⋊
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi y
                          %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ⋉
                              %mi x
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ⋉
                              %mi y
                              %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi y
                              %mo ⋊
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi y
                          %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {
                  x \otimes x'                      &amp; \overset{x \rtimes f'}\to  &amp; x \otimes y' \\
                  \\mathllap{f \ltimes x'}\downarrow &amp;                            &amp; \downarrow\mathrlap{f \ltimes y'} \\
                  y \otimes x'                      &amp; \underset{y \rtimes f'}\to &amp; y \otimes y' \\
                  }
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ⋊
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ⋉
                              %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ⋉
                              %mi y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi y
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ⋊
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {
                  x' \otimes x                      &amp; \overset{x' \rtimes f}\to  &amp; x' \otimes y \\
                  \\mathllap{f' \ltimes x}\downarrow &amp;                            &amp; \downarrow\mathrlap{f' \ltimes y} \\
                  y' \otimes x                      &amp; \underset{y' \rtimes f}\to &amp; y' \otimes y \\
                  }
          %p
            commute. In this case, we denote the common composites
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi y
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \otimes f'\colon x \otimes x' \to y \otimes y'
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f' \otimes f\colon x' \otimes x \to y' \otimes y
          %p
            A
            %strong premonoidal category
            is a binoidal category equipped with:
          %ul
            %li
              an object
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %li
              for each triple
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
              of objects, a central
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi z
                      %mo →
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_{x,y,z}\colon (x \otimes y) \otimes z \to x \otimes (y \otimes z)
            %li
              for each object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_x\colon x \otimes I \to x
              and
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ρ
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_x\colon I \otimes x \to x
          %p such that the following conditions hold.
          %ul
            %li
              all possible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality squares
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              (which make sense since we have central morphisms) commute. Note that when written out explicitly in terms of the functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\rtimes -
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ⋉
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\ltimes x
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              as a single natural transformation using the slick version below.)
            %li
              the pentagon law holds for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %li
              the triangle law holds for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
          %p
            A
            %strong strict premonoidal category
            is a premonoidal category in which
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \otimes y) \otimes z = x \otimes (y \otimes z)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes I = x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \otimes x = x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_{x,y,z}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_x
            are all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict category
            for this to make sense.)
          %p
            Similarly, a
            %strong symmetric premonoidal category
            is a premonoidal category equipped with a central natural isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\otimes y \cong y\otimes x
            (as for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          %h2#slick_version Slick version
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+monoidal+category"} strict monoidal category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ,
                    %mo □
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Cat,\Box)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo □
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/funny+tensor+product"} funny tensor product
          %p
            From this point of view, a binoidal category is just a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo □
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \Box C \to C
          %p
            We might hope that non-strict premonoidal categories are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonoids"} pseudomonoids
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo ,
                  %mo □
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Cat,\Box)
            seen as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+2-category"} monoidal 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unnatural+transformations"} unnatural transformations
            as 2-cells. For the requirement that coherence maps are natural, suggests taking
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
          %p
            %a{:href => "#R22"} Román 22
            provides the solution, showing that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freyd+categories"} Freyd categories
            (or
            = succeed ")," do
              %em effectful categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/promonads"} promonads
            equipped with their
            %em pure tensor product
            (described in Section 4 of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#R22"} Román 22
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
                is a premonoidal category.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} left- and right-strong monad
                on a monoidal category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                (e.g. a strong monad on a braided monoidal category), then the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_T
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                inherits a premonoidal structure, such that the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C_T
                is a strict premonoidal functor. This premonoidal structure is only a monoidal structure if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monad"} commutative monad
            %li
              %p
                A strict premonoidal category is the same as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquicategory"} sesquicategory
                with one object, so any object of a sesquicategory has a corresponding premonoidal category whose objects are endomorphisms and arrows are 2-cells.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The central morphisms of a premonoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(C)
            %strong centre
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint+functor"} right adjoint functor
            to the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MonCat
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PreMonCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MonCat \hookrightarrow PreMonCat
            using the definition of functor of premonoidal categories in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#PR97"} Power-Robinson 97
          %p
            In the same way that a (strict) monoidal category can be identified with a (strict)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            with one object, a strict premonoidal category can be identified with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquicategory"} sesquicategory
            with one object. In fact, a sesquicategory is precisely a category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over the monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Cat,\otimes)
            described above.
          %h2#morphisms Morphisms
          %p
            A notion of (non-strict)
            %em premonoidal functor
            is somewhat tricky to define. Part of the definition is clear: it should be a functor that preserves the tensor product up to specified coherent
            %em central
            isomorphism. However, the tricky part is whether it should also be required to preserve centrality of morphisms (or even just isomorphisms). Desiderata pulling in opposite directions include:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                If a premonoidal functor is not required to preserve centrality at least of isomorphisms, then premonoidal functors may not be closed under composition, since we may not be able to define central coherence isomorphisms for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \circ F
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                does not preserve the centrality of the coherence isomorphisms for
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %li
              %p
                A morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1 \to T_2
                of bistrong monads on a monoidal category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                induces a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{T_1} \to C_{T_2}
                which preserves the premonoidal structures
                = succeed "," do
                  %em strictly
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#SL13"} SL13
          %p
            It seems unlikely that these desiderata can be reconciled purely in the world of premonoidal categories as usually defined. One solution is to pass to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freyd-categories"} Freyd-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{T_1} \to C_{T_2}
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is cartesian (and if it isn’t, then there should be a suitable non-cartesian generalization of Freyd-categories). Other solutions that use different ways of representing a “special subfamily of central (iso)morphisms” are to consider the tensor product functor of a premonoidal category to be a not-necessarily-saturated
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precategory"} precategory
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premulticategory"} premulticategory
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freyd+category"} Freyd category
          %h2#references References
          %p Premonoidal categories were introduced in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Stuart Oliver Anderson, and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+J.+Power"} A. J. Power
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A representable approach to finite nondeterminism
            %li#PR97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Power"} John Power
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edmund+Robinson"} Edmund Robinson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Premonoidal categories and notions of computation
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.eecs.qmul.ac.uk/~edmundr/pubs/mscs97/premoncat.ps"} PostScript
          %p Further work in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Alan Jeffrey,
                %em Premonoidal categories and a graphical view of programs,
                %a{:href => "https://web.archive.org/web/20120303033606if_/http://fpl.cs.depaul.edu/ajeffrey/papers/premonA.pdf"} pdf file
            %li#SL13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sam+Staton"} Sam Staton
                and Paul Blain Levy,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Universal Properties of Impure Programming Languages
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1145/2480359.2429091"} doi
            %li#R22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Rom%C3%A1n"}> Mario Román
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Promonads and String Diagrams for Effectful Categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.380.20"} doi
        .revisedby
